  "worked_solution": "First, let's rewrite the system to reveal the coefficients:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x+(-3)y+1z=5 \\\\ 1x+1y+(-2)z=-3 \\\\ -5x+0y+4z=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe start by writing the determinant of the coefficients matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find ${D}_{y},$ we take the coefficients matrix, replace the second column by the right-hand side of the system, and calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y}=|\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -5 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}| & =5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}|-5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -5 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =5(-12-2)-5(4-10)+(-1-15) \\\\  & =-70+30-16 \\\\  & =-56.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying Cramer's rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{-56}{7}=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
